Some think the reply may have been to tell us that we're on the right track, communicating in the universal language of the cosmos binary code.
A German mathematician, Gottfried Leibniz, is credited with defining binary code in the 17th century.
In turn, Leibniz is said to have credited his inspiration to the 5,000-year-old Chinese text of I Ching, an ancient oracle code used to communicate divine guidance.
