We are heading into our 22nd season of "Survivor."
And we're doing it with a twist that will change the game.
For 21 seasons, "survivors" lived by one simple rule:
When someone is voted out, they're out of the game.
Their shot at the money is gone.
But that's about to change.
This time, when someone is voted out, they're not going home.
Instead, they'll be forced to live alone... on Redemption Island.
When the next person is voted out, they'll be sent to Redemption Island as well.
And the two will square off in a head-to-head duel where the only way to stay alive is to win.
One person will survive long enough to re-enter the game for shot at redemption and the million-dollar prize.
Those who voted them out may not be so happy to see them back.
It's the biggest twist in "Survivor" history.
Creating new obstacles, forcing new strategies.
Who will have what it takes to outwit, outplay, and outlast all the rest?
